		{ CGIFreeText 
			- _id = GUID 7e32e0b5-0891-4c79-a19d-33f6075d5610;
			- m_type = 46;
			- m_pModelObject = { IHandle 
				- _m2Class = "";
			}
			- m_pParent = GUID 1cceb05e-5bff-48d0-a091-c0a91d11a2dd;
			- m_name = { CGIText 
				- m_str = "This is a variant of the original HomeAlarm sample, redesigned using ports.

Ports are a new UML2.0 modeling concept that allows strong encapsulation of classes from the
environment. In this case, the Hardware and Alarm Controller are decoupled by specifying ports
as their boundary interaction points.

This sample also demonstrates the usage of the new Rhapsody 5.0 Requirement modeling concept - the AlarmPkg 
contains a set of requirements defined for the Home Alarm system. These requirements are realized by the use cases 
using <<trace>> dependencies as shown in the Requirements Vs. Use Cases diagram.

It is recommended to refer to the original sample in order to compare the traditional class-based approach vs
the port-based approach.

";
				- m_style = "Arial" 10 0 0 0 1 ;
				- m_color = { IColor 
					- m_fgColor = 32;
					- m_bgColor = 32;
					- m_bgFlag = 0;
				}
				- m_position = 1 3 13.7315789473684  ;
				- m_nIdent = 0;
				- m_bImplicitSetRectPoints = 0;
				- m_nOrientationCtrlPt = 8;
			}
			- m_drawBehavior = 4096;
			- m_bIsPreferencesInitialized = 1;
			- m_points = 4 52 77  827 77  827 320  52 320  ;
			- m_text = "This is a variant of the original HomeAlarm sample, redesigned using ports.

Ports are a new UML2.0 modeling concept that allows strong encapsulation of classes from the
environment. In this case, the Hardware and Alarm Controller are decoupled by specifying ports
as their boundary interaction points.

This sample also demonstrates the usage of the new Rhapsody 5.0 Requirement modeling concept - the AlarmPkg 
contains a set of requirements defined for the Home Alarm system. These requirements are realized by the use cases 
using <<trace>> dependencies as shown in the Requirements Vs. Use Cases diagram.

It is recommended to refer to the original sample in order to compare the traditional class-based approach vs
the port-based approach.

";
		}
